    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0365" n="351" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg351"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/10–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-09T13:00:00+01:00">October 9, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 9—9:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8491. Comea 109. Through its acting representative on the European Advisory
                    Commission, Sobolev,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d171-f1"/> the Soviet Government has
                    agreed to amend the draft protocol on zones of occupation in Germany in
                    accordance with the arrangement worked out at Quebec three weeks ago between the
                    United States and United Kingdom Governments. The text advanced by the British
                    delegation and amendments to incorporate these changes in the protocol was
                    forwarded in my 8137 [<hi rendition="#italic">8237</hi>], (September 29, 5 p.m.,
                    Comea 102). Department’s 8098 October 3, midnight, Eacom 33, reported that the
                    text of the delineation of the United States and United Kingdom zones had not
                    yet been approved by the Combined Chiefs of Staff. Lacking clearance on these
                    amendments, action in the EAC is at a standstill because the United States
                    delegation is not in a position to present its proposals for amendment <pb
                        facs="0366" n="352" xml:id="pg352"/> and thus to complete the essential
                    tripartite agreement on zones of occupation. Gousev is temporarily absent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d171-f1" n="1" xml:id="d171-f1-content">
                <p>Arkady Aleksandrovich Sobolev, Soviet Minister-Counselor in the United
                    Kingdom.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
